{=============================================================================
  Helium bottle pushing liquid oxygen at constant pressure (rocket exercise)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0283
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  In a rocket, a helium bottle pushes liquid oxygen (LOX) towards the engine
  pump at a constant pressure of 100 kPa. The LOX tank (5000 kg, 1142 kg/m^3)
  empties; the isobaric boundary work of the helium is -p*DeltaV. At the end
  the helium at -75 C and 100 kPa fills the bottle and the empty LOX tank;
  together with the initial state (20 C, 14 MPa) this gives the bottle volume.
  He is an ideal-gas substance in EES and in CoolSolve; with (T, P) inputs
  CoolSolve returns the real-fluid state (CS-GAP-IDEAL-GAS-MODEL, see README).
  Teaching exercise (ULiège course); the file names no author.

  Inputs : rho_LOX, m_LOX, p_LOX (p_alim), p_he_i, T_he_i, p_he_f, T_he_f
  Outputs: W, Vol_tank, Vol_ballon, m_he
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège course, file R2_E5_2022.EES (inventory TM-0401) - see README.md
  Licence: MIT. Status: verified against the EES stored solution (CS-GAP-IDEAL-GAS-MODEL on v_he_i).
============================================================================}

"!Data"
rho_LOX = 1142        "LOX density [kg/m^3], as in the original"
p_alim = 100E3        "supply pressure [Pa]; 100 kPa in the original; unused, as in the original"
p_he_i = 14E6         "initial helium pressure [Pa]; 14000 kPa in the original"
T_he_i = 20           "initial helium temperature [°C]; 20[K]+273.15 K in the original"
m_LOX = 5000          "LOX mass [kg], as in the original"
p_LOX = 100E3         "LOX delivery pressure [Pa]; 100 kPa in the original"
p_he_f = 100E3        "final helium pressure [Pa]; 100 kPa in the original"
T_he_f = -75          "final helium temperature [°C]; -75[K]+273.15 K in the original"

"!a) Work done by the helium"
"Volume of the LOX tank"
Vol_tank = m_LOX/rho_LOX   "LOX tank volume [m^3]"
"The helium pushes the LOX at constant pressure towards the pump: the process is
isobaric and the work is the (constant) pressure times the volume change. That
volume change is, in absolute value, the LOX tank volume, the tank going from
completely full to completely empty (as in the original)."
Vol_i = 0                  "initial volume of the helium [m^3], as in the original"
Vol_f = Vol_tank           "final volume of the helium [m^3], as in the original"
DELTAV = Vol_f - Vol_i     "volume change of the helium [m^3]"
W = -p_LOX * DELTAV        "boundary work [J]; negative because it is done by the system and not supplied to it"

"!b) Volume of the helium bottle"
"At the final state the helium fills the bottle and the empty LOX tank at
-75 °C and 100 kPa; the helium mass is computed first."
Vol_total = Vol_ballon + Vol_tank   "total final volume of the helium [m^3]"
m_he = Vol_total / v_he_f           "helium mass [kg]"
v_he_f = Volume(He,T=T_he_f,P=p_he_f)  "final specific volume of the helium [m^3/kg]"
"At the initial state all the helium is concentrated in the bottle at
20 °C and 14 MPa."
v_he_i = Volume(He,T=T_he_i,P=p_he_i)  "initial specific volume of the helium [m^3/kg]"
Vol_ballon = m_he*v_he_i           "volume of the helium bottle [m^3]"
